From c497e7abe5c386250e4ecba2e634c085b6828726 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Rajan <7121943+kvnloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:35:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] docs(gateway): sync run-status, session-stream,
 session-store, multiplex and bot-delivery docs

Six gateway-facing docs statements no longer match main:

- programmatic-integration.md: the "Provider/agent failure" row listed only
  `completed: false`, `error`. The retry-exhausted and non-retryable paths in
  agent/turn_recovery.py set `partial` when reply text was already delivered
  (#119001), and terminal_run_status() carries it on `run.failed`.
- api-server.md: the /api/sessions/{id}/chat/stream row omitted
  `approval.request`. _register_session_stream_approval() enqueues it, keyed
  by the run id, and parks the run in `waiting_for_approval` until
  POST /v1/runs/{run_id}/approval resolves it.
- gateway-session-lifecycle.md: switch_session() gained
  `preserve_prompt_pin=True`; /resume (slash_commands_session.py) and the CLI
  handoff (run_startup.py) pass False.
- multiplexing-gateway.md, control plane: profiles.describe / configure and
  create's seeding bind the full runtime scope via _hermes_home_scope()
  (home + secrets + terminal), not only a HERMES_HOME override.
- multiplexing-gateway.md, secret scope: build_profile_secret_scope() now
  overlays the administrator-managed .env last with override, so a
  secondary does not resolve "from its own files only".
- bot-mode.md (+ zh-Hans): tools/bot_relay._hermes_cli() tries the
  install's published launcher (.hermes/bin/hermes) before the interpreter
  sibling and PATH.
